WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:02.390
- You just celebrated your
daughter's graduation.

00:00:02.390 --> 00:00:03.223
That's amazing.
(audience applauds)

00:00:03.223 --> 00:00:06.123
So are you and Catherine
ready to be empty nesters?

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:09.260
- Yeah, I think so.

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:12.200
I mean, we had a lovely experience.

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:13.980
It was a virtual graduation.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:16.780
We couldn't actually be in
the same room that she was in

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:20.950
because of COVID
protections and all of that.

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:23.710
And it was so wonderful,
and I'm so proud of her.

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:25.540
But I gotta tell you, Kelly,

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:27.900
it's a little rough when
you're going out the doors

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:30.500
and the other parents are
saying, "Oh, congratulations."

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:33.107
Say, "Thank you. Congratulations to you."

00:00:33.107 --> 00:00:36.200
"I see you must be so proud
of your granddaughter."

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:39.280
(group laughs)

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:42.106
- I said, "Well..." (laughs)

00:00:42.106 --> 00:00:42.939
- [Kelly] That's-

00:00:42.939 --> 00:00:44.980
- I don't know, man. I don't know.

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:46.040
Yeah. Okay.

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:47.910
I'm not gonna take it personal.

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:50.278
I think they're just trying
to be nice, but yeah.

00:00:50.278 --> 00:00:52.040
- [Kelly] Just lean in.

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:55.610
- We were getting ready
for it, and we prepared,

00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:57.780
but then when the COVID happened

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:02.150
and we had everybody
back home this past year.

00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:03.540
But there is that moment

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:07.790
when they're gone and
they're out of the house

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:10.140
and they're gone and
you look at each other,

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:11.710
and in the back of your
mind you're thinking,

00:01:11.710 --> 00:01:13.795
what are we gonna talk about?

00:01:13.795 --> 00:01:14.628
(group laughs)

00:01:14.628 --> 00:01:16.268
What are we gonna talk about?

00:01:16.268 --> 00:01:18.131
I mean, I know-
- You get to date again.

00:01:18.131 --> 00:01:19.237
You get to date again!

00:01:19.237 --> 00:01:20.070
- Well, you do.

00:01:20.070 --> 00:01:21.642
Well, you can do all that.
- Yeah!

00:01:21.642 --> 00:01:23.850
- But you really, as a marriage,

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:25.130
so much of your time revolves

00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:28.250
around talking about your
kids, what they're doing,

00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:29.850
how are they doing, and this and that.

00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:31.800
It's an easy conversation.

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:34.330
So I think we're gonna do real well.

00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:36.960
We got our suitcases packed.

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:38.280
The COVID's getting down.

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:39.950
We're looking to do a lot of traveling

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:41.730
the next couple of years, moving around.

00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:43.640
I'm gonna be working over here in Europe

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:45.590
for a lot of this next year.

00:01:45.590 --> 00:01:47.660
So we'll be okay.
- Wow!

00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:49.170
That's excite, I know I always love that.

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:50.520
I think you get to start dating again.

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:51.470
I think that's fun.

